Mac par (Terminal kholein)

Zip extract karne ke baad:

cd ~/Desktop/final-expense-app
npm install
npm run build
nano .env

.env mein ye likhein:

HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=5180

Ctrl+O, Enter, Ctrl+X se save.

Phir:

npm test
npm start

(cd ka path wahi likhein jahan extract kiya. Agar Node install nahi to pehle nodejs.org se LTS lein.)

Start hote hi terminal mein teen URL dikhenge — Claude Code ne ye feature banaya tha:

On this machine: http://localhost:5180
From other machines: http://<Mac-ka-naam>.local:5180
From other machines (if the name fails): http://192.168.x.x:5180

Baqi laptops par

Bas browser mein wo doosra URL kholein, jaise http://Kayce-MacBook.local:5180. Kuch install nahi karna. Har banda apne account se login karega.

Agar .local wala naam Windows laptops par na chale to teesra wala (IP) use karein.

Kuch cheezein pehli baar Mac par:

Firewall permission ka popup aayega — Allow dabayein.
Mac ka naam dekhne ke liye: System Settings → General → Sharing → "Local hostname".
Mac sota na rahe: System Settings → Battery → charger par "Prevent automatic sleeping" on.
Sab laptops ek hi WiFi par hon.

Yaad rahe: Mac par database khali hoga. Users, passwords, appointed states, questions — sab naye se set karne honge. docs/LAN_SETUP.md mein baqi tafseel hai (backup, auto-start).

Terminal band karne se server band ho jayega. Us ko background mein chalane ka tareeqa LAN_SETUP.md mein hai.
